🌍 Land Management System
The Land Management System enables users to register different types of land such as Agricultural, Residential, Commercial, and Industrial. The system uses a Scanner for input and validates fields like land ID (numeric), owner name, location (alphabetic), and land use status. Based on the user's land type selection, additional attributes are collected (e.g., number of units for residential land, commercial zone status, environmental clearance). Each registered land entry is stored in a List<Land>, and a report is generated immediately after registration. At the end, the system prints all registered land reports. Validation methods ensure proper data types are entered.

🪖 Mission Management System
The Mission Management System facilitates the management of military or organizational missions. It prompts the user to enter details for personnel and resources, validating inputs like ID (digits), names (letters only), and quantities (positive integers). After gathering a list of personnel and resources, users choose one of four mission types: Recon, Rescue, Combat, or Humanitarian. The system collects mission-specific details including ID, name, start/end dates, and mission status. It checks that the end date is not earlier than the start date. Once the mission is created, tasks are assigned, resources are allocated, progress is tracked, and a mission report is generated.

🏫 Nursery School Management System
The Nursery School Management System allows administrators to manage different nursery classes: Baby Class, Middle Class, and Top Class. Users can assign teachers, enroll students, conduct activities, and—specifically for the Top Class—add assessments. The system uses a Map<Integer, NurseryClass> to dynamically access and manipulate the appropriate class based on user input. It includes input validation for IDs (digits), names (letters), and age (integer). Each action (assignment, enrollment, etc.) is performed through method calls on class-specific objects. Reports can be generated to track progress or review overall class activity.
